Warning cleanup: unused locals (clang -Wunused-variable, -Wunused-but-set-variable, -Wunused-function).

Locals whose initializers have no side effects are removed: conversion.cpp bytes_per_block, xam_user.cpp size and
o, mmio_handler.cpp rex_w, object_table.cpp result, xex_module.cpp mem_size, input_size, sec_header and data,
settings_overlay.cpp display_label, virtual_file_system.cpp created (set, never read) and packet_disassembler.cpp
address (set, never read). Locals that read guest memory (xboxkrnl_debug.cpp, kept for inspection at the debug
break, and xam_app.cpp), are only used when FidelityFX is built in (presenter.cpp), or are the only use of a
parameter (xex_module.cpp exe_length, xam_content.cpp content_data; removing them would only move the warning to
the parameter) are marked [[maybe_unused]] instead, so nothing about their evaluation changes. The unused static
LifecycleBadge() in settings_overlay.cpp is marked [[maybe_unused]] too.

